 ## Overview
-BSP-XMPVO is a visibility sorting algorithm for unstructured and curvilinear grids that combines a Binary Space Partition (BSP) tree of exterior faces with the adjacency-based ordering of MPVO to handle non-convex meshes [S1, S5][S7, unofficial]. It augments the partial order from MPVO with dependencies derived from the BSP tree to resolve occlusions between non-adjacent cells, achieving exact sorting with linear time complexity relative to the number of cells, $O(n + bp)$, where $n$ is the total cells, $b$ is the boundary cells, and $p$ is the small number of partially projected cells [S5][S7, unofficial]. Unlike MPVO, which assumes convexity and produces artifacts on non-convex meshes, BSP-XMPVO provides exact ordering for general acyclic meshes [S3, unofficial][S5].
+BSP-XMPVO is a visibility sorting algorithm for unstructured and curvilinear grids that combines a Binary Space Partition (BSP) tree of exterior faces with the adjacency-based ordering of MPVO to handle non-convex meshes [S1, S5][S7, unofficial]. It augments the partial order from MPVO with dependencies derived from the BSP tree to resolve occlusions between non-adjacent cells, achieving exact sorting with linear time complexity relative to the number of cells, $O(n + bp)$, where $n$ is the total cells, $b$ is the boundary cells, and $p$ is the small number of partially projected cells [S1, S5][S7, unofficial]. Unlike MPVO, which assumes convexity and produces artifacts on non-convex meshes, BSP-XMPVO provides exact ordering for general acyclic meshes [S3, unofficial][S5].
 
